# PostgreSQL custom image and PG18 logical migrate

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Image bake (`services-conf/db.Dockerfile`)

| Law | Detail |
|-----|--------|
| Base | Pinned **`alpine:3.24.x`** (e.g. `3.24.2`). **Forbidden:** `alpine:latest`, `alpine:edge`, `debian:trixie` for the DB image |
| Stack | Source-build under `/opt`: jemalloc, **zlib-ng (ZLIB_COMPAT)**, liburing, lz4, zstd; PostgreSQL 18.x SHA pin; TimescaleDB 2.31.x **without** `APACHE_ONLY`. **Forbidden:** linking postgres/zstd to apk `zlib` / `zlib-dev` ABI (`ldd` must show `/opt/zlib-ng`). apk `zlib` may still exist as a transitive dep of openssl/libxml2 — do **not** fail-closed on `apk info -e zlib` |
| Configure | `--without-icu --with-liburing --with-lz4 --with-zstd --with-llvm` (+ openssl/libxml/libxslt/uuid as documented). **No ICU** (removed 2026-11-11): every DB uses the libc provider and nothing uses an ICU collation, while each ICU major changes collator versions (REINDEX risk). Fail-closed: `ldd postgres` must show no `libicu`; do not re-add ICU, `/opt/icu` or `icu-data-full` without a feature that needs ICU collations. Postgres and zstd CLI link `/opt/zlib-ng` + `/opt/lz4`. **`timescaledb.so` must not DT_NEEDED jemalloc** (or external lz4/zstd on 2.29+) — allocator comes from the postgres process (`LD_PRELOAD` + postgres DT_NEEDED). **unset LDFLAGS alone is insufficient** (Timescale uses `pg_config --ldflags`); write a `pg_config` wrap with **`printf`** inside `RUN` (no shell `<<EOF` heredoc — podman/buildah misparses it as `CHMOD`) and sed link.txt. Alpine BusyBox sed: **do not** use `s|…|…|` when the pattern contains `|` (OR); use `#` delimiters / plain `s/-ljemalloc//g`. Fail-closed: `if grep …; then exit 1; fi` on `scanelf -n` (bash `set -e` ignores `! grep` when the pattern matches). Do not fail-closed musl `ldd` greps requiring `/opt/lz4` on the extension. **Do not** pass docker-library `--disable-rpath`. **Do not** pass removed PG18 flags such as `--enable-thread-safety` |
| CFLAGS | **Clang 22** apk (`clang22`, **`compiler-rt`**, `llvm22-dev`, `lld22`); **`CC=clang`**. **`lld22`** installs **`ld.lld`** at **`/usr/bin/ld.lld`** (not under **`/usr/lib/llvm22/bin/`**). Postgres + Timescale: `-O2 -march=native -mprefer-vector-width=512 -mtune=native -flto=thin --ld-path=/usr/bin/ld.lld -g0` via **`services-conf/bake_clang_flags.sh`**. Supporting `/opt` libs: same ThinLTO baseline without 512-bit prefer. LZ4 bake also passes **`-DLZ4_HEAPMODE=0`**. No custom Clang profile-guided rebuild path. |
| Runtime | `LD_PRELOAD` jemalloc on musl; fail-closed `ldd` shows `/opt/...` for jemalloc/**zlib-ng**/uring/lz4/zstd on **`postgres`** and zlib-ng+lz4 on **`zstd` CLI**; do not apk-add `zlib` ourselves (transitive apk zlib OK). Entrypoints **`services-conf/db-docker-entrypoint.sh`** + **`db-docker-ensure-initdb.sh`** must be **git-tracked** (`!services-conf/db-docker-*.sh` under root `*.sh` ignore) — bake `COPY` fails on prod if they are ignored. Host bind for `postgres_data_pg18` must be **`chown -R 70:70`** (Alpine postgres) before first start — bind replaces image `1777`; empty `root:root` / NFS `root_squash` → `mkdir …/18/` Permission denied |
| Build host | Bake on the **prod CPU** (`native`). Cross-arch (e.g. aarch64) images are not the ship target for x86_64 production |
| Toolchain image | **Removed** — no **`gcc-alpine.Dockerfile`** / musl GCC pre-build. **`db-build`** and **`proxy-build`** install **`clang22`** in-image; **`rebuild_full_site.sh`** **`podman build`**s **web**, **proxy**, **`db_pg18`**, then compose **`up -d --no-build**. |

## Compose dual-run

- Keep Hub **`timescale/timescaledb:2.28.3-pg15`** as service **`db`** (alias **`db`**) until cutover.
- Homemade service **`db_pg18`** (`image: hpcperfstats-db`), profile **`pg18-migrate`**, alias **`db18`**, volume **`postgres_data_pg18`**, mount **`/var/lib/postgresql`**, same `shm_size: "16gb"` GUCs **plus** `-c io_method=io_uring`, **`security_opt: [seccomp=unconfined, label=disable]`**, and **`cap_add: [SYS_ADMIN]`**. Host io_uring: preferred **`kernel.io_uring_disabled=1`** + **`kernel.io_uring_group=70`** (Alpine postgres gid); alternative **`disabled=0`**; **forbidden** **`disabled=2`**. With **`disabled=1`** and unset group (`-1`), uid 70 gets **EPERM** even with seccomp unconfined.
- **`db_pg18` runtime GUCs match `db`** (`shared_buffers=64GB`, WAL/bgwriter, committed **`hba_file`** + `postgres_pg_hba.conf` mount): it becomes production `db` at cutover and the overlay cannot override `command:` (podman-compose ignores it). Dual-run **must not** mount `postgres_runtime` on `db_pg18` (two servers in one socket dir collide on `.s.PGSQL.5432.lock`).
- **Cutover = tracked `docker-compose.pg18-primary.yaml` added to the site `docker-compose.yaml` `include:` list** (parks `db` under profile `pg15-retired`, `profiles: !reset []` + alias `db` + `postgres_runtime` on `db_pg18`). **Forbidden:** a `docker-compose.override.yaml` cutover — `-f docker-compose.yaml` skips it and revives PG15 as `db`. `rebuild_full_site.sh` resolves the live DB service (`compose_primary_db_service`).
- **Forbidden:** stealing alias `db` before freeze + verification.
- Migration/cutover `up` commands **name services**: after any compose-file edit a bare `podman-compose up -d` recreates every project container (stale config hash), including `rabbitmq`/`valkey`.
- Both DB containers keep **`shm_size: "16gb"`** during dual-run (`postgres-docker-shared-memory.mdc`).

## Logical migrate (not `pg_upgrade`)

- Fresh Django hypertable on PG18; **do not** restore `_timescaledb_catalog` from PG15.
- `host_data` copy (`scripts/pg18_host_data_chunk_copy.py`, run from a one-shot `web` with the checkout script mounted): **binary** COPY with an explicit column list that must match source/target names **and** types (fail closed). Per chunk: read the source **signature** first (`pg_stat_all_tables` ins/upd/del of the chunk + its compressed relation — Hub 2.28 `_timescaledb_catalog.chunk` shape, source only), skip when counts match, else decompress target + delete + COPY + recount. **`--state-file`** + **`--changed-only`**: chunks whose signature is unchanged since verification get no query. **Slice resync** (`--slice-minutes 60`): a changed chunk whose upd/del counters did not move since its record re-copies only mismatched slices (ingest is `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`); any UPDATE/DELETE → whole chunk. **`--compress-older-than-days 8`** compresses copied target chunks immediately (policy stays removed until cutover). **`--verify`** (freeze) recounts both sides and exits non-zero. A failed chunk is logged, dropped from state, and the run continues (exit 1). Counts retry `Operation canceled` / `QueryCanceled`.
- **Chunk creation never inside a COPY transaction.** TimescaleDB holds `ShareUpdateExclusiveLock` on the hypertable from chunk creation until the creating transaction ends; a day chunk created inside its COPY serialized every other worker behind the longest COPY (hpcperfstats04 2026-11-11: three workers blocked 31 h, effective 1 worker at ~1.6k rows/s). `precreate_target_chunks` inserts + deletes `__pg18_chunk_precreate__` placeholder rows (autocommit) per target chunk interval first; skipped when a target chunk already overlaps. **All** of a run's missing target chunks are pre-created **up front** (`precreate_all_target_chunks`) because `compress_chunk` also blocks chunk creation while it runs (TS 2.31: new-chunk insert waited out a 29 s compress).
- **Compression off the copy workers:** finished chunks past `--compress-older-than-days` go to a background pool (`--compress-workers`, default 2); the worker moves on. Compress failures are logged and never fail a verified chunk. Each non-freeze run also compresses aged uncompressed target chunks; `--verify` (freeze) never compresses.
- **Freeze gate:** `--verify` exits 2 (`refusing --verify`) unless every saved index is back and valid **and** `host_data` has a valid UNIQUE index (ingest `ON CONFLICT`); runbook E1 also refuses to stop PG15 without a valid UNIQUE index on PG18.
- **Rerunnable:** the same start command re-syncs newer days at any time (new chunks copied, unchanged ones skipped without queries, aged ones compressed).
- **PG18 indexes dropped for the bulk copy:** `--drop-target-indexes` saves `pg_get_indexdef` of every non-constraint `host_data` index to `<state stem>.indexes.json` (never overwritten) and drops them; `--restore-target-indexes --maintenance-work-mem 2GB` (runbook C2, after the bulk copy, before D1, copy not running) recreates missing **or invalid** ones: non-unique with `timescaledb.transaction_per_chunk` (before any `WHERE`), UNIQUE plain (TimescaleDB rejects per-chunk for UNIQUE), then fails closed on any invalid `host_data` index. Rebuilding UNIQUE with compressed chunks works on 2.31 and still enforces uniqueness / `ON CONFLICT`.
- **Forbidden:** full-table `count(*) FROM host_data` gates during the freeze window (decompresses all of PG15) — the freeze pass `verified_rows=` total is the gate.
- Relational tables at freeze: **`scripts/pg18_relational_copy.sh`** inside `db_pg18` (same table set check, parallel `pg_dump -Fd` / `pg_restore --data-only --disable-triggers`, exact per-table counts, ANALYZE). No hand-maintained TRUNCATE list.
- Freeze order and verify steps: **`docs/OPERATOR_PG18_MIGRATION.md`**.
- **Forbidden:** `pg_dump -t host_data` alone; cutover without freeze; `host_data` UPDATE/DELETE repair tools between the catch-up pass and the freeze pass.

